[5.706189,"o","BusyBox v1.20.2 (Debian 1:1.20.0-7) multi-call binary.\n"]
[5.706218,"o","Copyright (C) 1998-2011 Erik Andersen, Rob Landley, Denys Vlasenko\n"]
[5.706241,"o","and others. Licensed under GPLv2.\n"]
[5.706261,"o","See source distribution for full notice.\n"]
[5.706281,"o","\n"]
[5.706303,"o","Usage: busybox [function] [arguments]...\n"]
[5.706321,"o","   or: busybox --list[-full]\n"]
[5.706339,"o","   or: busybox --install [-s] [DIR]\n"]
[5.706357,"o","   or: function [arguments]...\n"]
[5.706374,"o","\n"]
[5.706392,"o","    BusyBox is a multi-call binary that combines many common Unix\n"]
[5.706428,"o","    utilities into a single executable.  Most people will create a\n"]
[5.706462,"o","    link to busybox for each function they wish to use and BusyBox\n"]
[5.706481,"o","    will act like whatever it was invoked as.\n"]
